# Frontend architecture

Follow `docs/frontend-architecture.md`.

- Put feature code in `frontend/src/features/<feature>/`. `app/` only composes a page from that feature.
- UI and server actions call a feature service. The service depends on a repository interface, not `fetch`.
- Repositories live in `features/<feature>/data/` and use `shared/api` for HTTP. They do not set cookies, render, or own form validation.
- Phone rules, copy, and session storage stay in their own modules.
- Shared visuals stay in `components/ui`. Do not put feature API calls there.
- Add a new repository per feature. Do not extend one global API object.

```tsx
const result = await requestOneTimeCode(repository, phone)
```

```tsx
// page or component calling fetch
await fetch("/api/auth/otp/request")
```
